## 4. The cljd REPL starts
With HEAD at `7e14a91`, I ran `clj -M:cljd-yin-repl --telemetry < /dev/null`:
```
Compiling ClojureDart namespace...
ClojureDart compilation successful. Starting Dart REPL...
--telemetry and --telemetry-stream are not part of the DaoStream v2 REPL slice; v2 telemetry is owed to its own plan (yin.vm.telemetry.implementation-plan.md, not yet written)
yin> Bye
```
There's no `run_main` error. The Dart REPL starts, rejects `--telemetry` with text that names no v1 program, and exits when input ends.

I ran interactive mode rather than `--headless`. A headless run with `--port 18097` stays up serving, which is what it should do, but my output filter held everything until the process exited, so I couldn't read its startup lines. I stopped it after 180 seconds and checked that no process was left behind. The interactive run goes through the same compile-and-start path.
